-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Moley Christmas
  Publisher   Gremlin / Your Sinclair, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Moley Christmas (1987)(Gremlin Graphics Software - Your
              Sinclair).z80
  MD5         3a40c5f27fb88a7f36553d75e059d732

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.0: Monty, the enemies and the pickups as Next sprites;
              Infinite lives covers both ways of losing a life

  Note        Keys: Z left, X right, O up, K down, Space jump; Sinclair and
              Kempston joysticks work without choosing them. Monty, the
              enemies and the pickups are Next sprites in their own colours,
              so they no longer take on the scenery's colours; the screen
              underneath stays exactly as the game draws it, because the game
              checks it for collisions. Known issues: the picture changes more
              often per game update than the original's (2.24 against 1.04),
              so overlapping figures may flicker. Missing: a real Next run.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives

  Cheats are the archive's POKEs for this release, both writes, checked on the
  ordinary and the trap death. A widely shared tape copy already has one of
  them applied; this patch needs the clean TOSEC file.

